It was still worth publishing the book.

00:03:44.287 --> 00:03:46.040
The book itself is amazing.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:47.393
And

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.750
I've come to live with the cover.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:50.583
Next up,

00:03:50.583 --> 00:03:51.416
Ops Endless,

00:03:51.416 --> 00:03:53.204
does it have to be three
words for the credo

00:03:53.204 --> 00:03:55.003
or can it be three statements?

00:03:55.003 --> 00:03:57.691
The idea with the credo is
that it represents three ideas.

00:03:57.691 --> 00:03:59.229
You have your one word

00:03:59.229 --> 00:04:01.273
whether it's believe, whether it's family,

00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:03.513
whether it's extraordinary,
whether it's belong,

00:04:03.513 --> 00:04:05.377
whatever it is, you have your one word.

00:04:05.377 --> 00:04:07.199
And then the credo helps you

00:04:07.199 --> 00:04:10.265
add more definition to it for yourself

00:04:10.265 --> 00:04:12.465
and also for other people looking at it

00:04:12.465 --> 00:04:14.804
whether they're your customers
or suppliers or employees,

00:04:14.804 --> 00:04:16.424
partners, your investors.

00:04:16.424 --> 00:04:19.227
So they have a little better
understanding of what it means.

00:04:19.227 --> 00:04:22.815
And so, the credo represents
three different concepts.

00:04:22.815 --> 00:04:24.510
It could be three different words.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:25.625
It could be

00:04:25.625 --> 00:04:26.693
three different statements.

00:04:26.693 --> 00:04:27.891
Although I wanted

00:04:27.891 --> 00:04:29.897
I wanted you to make sure
they're easy to remember.

00:04:29.897 --> 00:04:33.113
They're not these long sentences.

00:04:33.113 --> 00:04:33.946
Because what happens,

00:04:33.946 --> 00:04:36.202
it's always a tendency to
make it longer and longer

00:04:36.202 --> 00:04:37.752
and longer and longer

00:04:37.752 --> 00:04:39.262
and then you don't remember it.

00:04:39.262 --> 00:04:41.386
I want these three things to be memorable.

00:04:41.386 --> 00:04:43.186
So that if somebody asks
you what your credo is

00:04:43.186 --> 00:04:44.736
you don't have to

00:04:44.736 --> 00:04:47.522
open your notebook and find it.

00:04:47.522 --> 00:04:49.060
You know it.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:49.893
And so

00:04:49.893 --> 00:04:50.738
that's the danger.

00:04:50.738 --> 00:04:52.114
That's the risk.

00:04:52.114 --> 00:04:53.838
If you make them long statements,

00:04:53.838 --> 00:04:54.841
then you're not going to remember them.

00:04:54.841 --> 00:04:56.792
If you don't remember them
then what's the point?

00:04:56.792 --> 00:04:58.632
The whole point is that
it's easy to remember

00:04:58.632 --> 00:05:00.223
so that you can start to live by it

00:05:00.223 --> 00:05:02.394
and other people can know you by it

00:05:02.394 --> 00:05:04.019
and they can know how to help you

00:05:04.019 --> 00:05:04.852
know how to interact with you

00:05:04.852 --> 00:05:06.457
know if they want to buy from you or not.

00:05:06.457 --> 00:05:08.487
That's a hesitation doesn't have to be

00:05:08.487 --> 00:05:09.729
three different words,

00:05:09.729 --> 00:05:12.173
but I would really
strongly recommend that you

00:05:12.173 --> 00:05:13.090
shrink it down.

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:14.054
Next up, nonstop.

00:05:14.054 --> 00:05:15.052
Hi Evan, I love your videos.

00:05:15.052 --> 00:05:17.775
Can you make a video about,
"how to spend your money best,

00:05:17.775 --> 00:05:18.825
"in your company?"

00:05:18.825 --> 00:05:22.041
So at the start, I'm not a
big fan of spending any money.

00:05:22.041 --> 00:05:25.327
I like to build stuff up
using my energy, my heart,

00:05:25.327 --> 00:05:26.395
my time,

00:05:26.395 --> 00:05:27.318
my effort

00:05:27.318 --> 00:05:29.605
and not spending money
until I'm making money.

00:05:29.605 --> 00:05:30.656
And so,

00:05:30.656 --> 00:05:32.891
it's thinking whether I spend my time to

00:05:32.891 --> 00:05:34.290
get some dollars coming in.

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.474
I had this big vision for
where I want to take something.

00:05:36.474 --> 00:05:37.467
You have this big vision for

00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:38.703
where you want to take something

00:05:38.703 --> 00:05:40.051
and you're starting here at the bottom.

00:05:40.051 --> 00:05:41.090
And it's okay.

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:43.488
A lot of people want to
take these giant steps,

00:05:43.488 --> 00:05:45.049
but if you try to take a giant step,

00:05:45.049 --> 00:05:46.692
you're going to make a lot of mistakes.

00:05:46.692 --> 00:05:49.351
And so if you take out
a mortgage on your house

00:05:49.351 --> 00:05:51.835
to take this big giant
step and it doesn't work,

00:05:51.835 --> 00:05:54.001
you might be in debt for
the rest of your life now

00:05:54.001 --> 00:05:55.736
because of this extra
loan that you took out.

00:05:55.736 --> 00:05:56.892
I don't want that for you.

00:05:56.892 --> 00:05:58.192
I want you to prove to yourself

00:05:58.192 --> 00:05:59.759
that it's worth spending your time,

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:01.219
worth spending more dollars

00:06:01.219 --> 00:06:02.052
in it.

00:06:02.052 --> 00:06:04.533
And so, at the beginning,
I'm spending zero dollars.

00:06:04.533 --> 00:06:05.433
Where should you spend your money?

00:06:05.433 --> 00:06:06.443
No where.

00:06:06.443 --> 00:06:07.918
Keep it in your bank account.

00:06:07.918 --> 00:06:09.259
Keep it in your investments.

00:06:09.259 --> 00:06:11.267
Until you get to the part
where you're making money.

00:06:11.267 --> 00:06:12.922
Once you start making money,

00:06:12.922 --> 00:06:15.244
you're investing a lot of
it back into your business

00:06:15.244 --> 00:06:17.856
and from there, I'm looking
at what is going to give me

00:06:17.856 --> 00:06:19.557
the highest return on my dollars?

00:06:19.557 --> 00:06:20.607
Just like you want to be thinking

00:06:20.607 --> 00:06:22.482
what's giving me the
highest return on my time?

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:23.609
Any resource you have,

00:06:23.609 --> 00:06:25.333
this is what being an
entrepreneur is all about.

00:06:25.333 --> 00:06:27.544
Any resource you have
is going to be limited.

00:06:27.544 --> 00:06:29.454
You have limited funds,
you have limited team.

00:06:29.454 --> 00:06:30.905
Maybe zero right now.

00:06:30.905 --> 00:06:31.891
You have limited time.

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:32.890
Everything is limited.

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:36.047
It's what do you do with
that limited resource?

00:06:36.047 --> 00:06:36.880
What do you do with your money?

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:37.713
What do you do with your time?

00:06:37.713 --> 00:06:38.863
What do you do with the
connections that you have?

00:06:38.863 --> 00:06:40.053
The friends, the family,

00:06:40.053 --> 00:06:42.427
maybe people in your team,
volunteers, whatever it is,

00:06:42.427 --> 00:06:44.865
how do you best use
all of those resources?

00:06:44.865 --> 00:06:46.363
What's going to generate
the biggest result

00:06:46.363 --> 00:06:48.000
for the least amount of input.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.014
And so, when you pour dollars on something

00:06:50.014 --> 00:06:52.272
you want it to be gasoline, right?

00:06:52.272 --> 00:06:54.485
So it's like, hey I've started
this marketing campaign

00:06:54.485 --> 00:06:55.355
it's working.

00:06:55.355 --> 00:06:57.045
Now if I put some money into it,

00:06:57.045 --> 00:06:59.083
it's going to work even more.

00:06:59.083 --> 00:06:59.916
Right?

00:06:59.916 --> 00:07:01.104
And you test it, and you
test it, and you test it,

00:07:01.104 --> 00:07:03.113
and you see what's working,
you find something,

00:07:03.113 --> 00:07:05.249
and I like to go all in on that

00:07:05.249 --> 00:07:07.751
dominate it, crush it, explode it,

00:07:07.751 --> 00:07:09.257
that's why I want folks to manage it

00:07:09.257 --> 00:07:10.308
because it's working.

00:07:10.308 --> 00:07:11.141
First, I'm making sure

00:07:11.141 --> 00:07:12.462
that I'm making some kind of money on it

00:07:12.462 --> 00:07:13.652
and then two, I'm looking at okay

00:07:13.652 --> 00:07:14.987
how do I

00:07:14.987 --> 00:07:16.601
find the thing that if
I put a dollar in it

00:07:16.601 --> 00:07:18.279
I'm getting five out.

00:07:18.279 --> 00:07:19.893
So, it could be a lot
of different activities.

00:07:19.893 --> 00:07:21.443
It speaks to where your strengths are,

00:07:21.443 --> 00:07:22.441
what your market is.

00:07:22.441 --> 00:07:23.904
There's no one answer that

00:07:23.904 --> 00:07:27.364
put all your money into Instagram ads.

00:07:27.364 --> 00:07:28.827
That may be a great strategy

00:07:28.827 --> 00:07:31.475
or it may not if you don't
know what you're doing.

00:07:31.475 --> 00:07:32.874
So, that's my advice.

00:07:32.874 --> 00:07:33.707
Good luck.

00:07:33.707 --> 00:07:36.212
Next up, The Howling Chihuahua.

00:07:36.212 --> 00:07:37.045
I love that name.

00:07:37.045 --> 00:07:38.447
Your One Word is a badass book

00:07:38.447 --> 00:07:40.298
because it inspired me to be fearless

00:07:40.298 --> 00:07:41.634
in my entrepreneur journey.

00:07:41.634 --> 00:07:43.096
Thanks EC and his people.

00:07:43.096 --> 00:07:44.246
I love that.

00:07:44.246 --> 00:07:45.563
That's why I wrote the book.

00:07:45.563 --> 00:07:48.559
I had tremendous success
using these strategies.

00:07:48.559 --> 00:07:50.625
And I was having success
with the people around me

00:07:50.625 --> 00:07:51.647
adopting those strategies.

00:07:51.647 --> 00:07:53.140
And I wanted to share it with you guys.

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:54.875
I wanted to share with entrepreneurs.

00:07:54.875 --> 00:07:56.054
I struggled so much

00:07:56.054 --> 00:07:58.654
in getting my first
business off the ground.

00:07:58.654 --> 00:07:59.949
And the reason I do all of this

00:07:59.949 --> 00:08:02.474
is I wanted to make your
journey a little bit easier.

00:08:02.474 --> 00:08:04.564
I'm kind of thinking back to myself

00:08:04.564 --> 00:08:07.037
trying to help the 19 year old Evan

00:08:07.037 --> 00:08:09.951
who's starting his first
business and sucking and failing

00:08:09.951 --> 00:08:11.513
and

00:08:11.513 --> 00:08:15.756
down and feeling worthless
because nothing was working out.

00:08:15.756 --> 00:08:17.852
And everything that I do is
kind of thinking back to that

00:08:17.852 --> 00:08:18.955
entrepreneur.

00:08:18.955 --> 00:08:20.750
Trying to help him

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:22.288
not quit because I did quit.

00:08:22.288 --> 00:08:24.227
And I came back, thankfully.

00:08:24.227 --> 00:08:25.823
But I wanted to make the
road a little more easier

00:08:25.823 --> 00:08:27.130
for

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:29.376
other entrepreneurs who
are going through it.

00:08:29.376 --> 00:08:30.885
And all the content that I make,

00:08:30.885 --> 00:08:32.203
that's the purpose.

00:08:32.203 --> 00:08:34.676
And when I discovered the
strategies that became the book,

00:08:34.676 --> 00:08:36.801
I need to share this, I
need to get this out there,

00:08:36.801 --> 00:08:38.049
people need to see this stuff.

00:08:38.049 --> 00:08:39.279
They need to apply it.

00:08:39.279 --> 00:08:40.736
And so it's awesome, what did you say?

00:08:40.736 --> 00:08:41.648
You're fearless

00:08:41.648 --> 00:08:42.774
in your entrepreneur journey.

00:08:42.774 --> 00:08:43.607
I love it.

